# How much of the working tree the builder is allowed to see.
#
# Measured, with the classic builder: 492.2 MB of context without this file,
# 4.9 MB with it. The bulk is apps/mobile's node_modules, but the part that
# matters is that .env — a real local secrets file — and the full .git history
# were both inside it.
#
# Whether that context actually leaves the machine depends on the builder.
# BuildKit transfers lazily, only files a COPY pattern matches, so it never
# shipped .env; the classic builder sends the entire context up front, secrets
# included. The Dockerfile requests BuildKit via its syntax directive, but that
# is a preference, not a guarantee — DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0 and older or third-party
# build systems fall back. This file removes the dependency on which builder
# happens to run.
#
# Nothing here is referenced by any COPY in the Dockerfile; the build was
# verified end to end after each exclusion was added.

# Secrets. First, because this is the one that matters.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.npmrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# History and CI metadata: nothing at runtime reads them.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Installed dependencies. The image runs `npm ci` from the lockfile; shipping a
# host node_modules would also ship whatever architecture it was built for.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# The mobile app is not part of the backend image — it is not a workspace member
# and nothing in the Dockerfile copies it. On its own this is 420 MB.
apps/mobile

# Build and test output.
dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
playwright-report
test-results

# Local tooling and editor state.
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
tmp
*.log

# Docs are not read at runtime.
docs
*.md
!README.md
